{"id":"XJAEOC2WS","name":"How?","paragraphs":[{"text":"1%md\n\n####SCALA or  Python","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"3b1231900d364dffb8210","status":404},{"text":"\n###SPARK","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"ff786409b3bc450a89a1b","status":404},{"text":"%spark\nval f:(Int => Int) = x => x*x\nval l:List[Int] = List(1,2,3,4,5,6)\nl.map(f)","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"584af33d0b3a48a3895e1","status":404},{"text":"\n####SQL\n","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"0660d5dcfb994f9f8d35c","status":404},{"text":"%spark\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions._\n\nval months = Seq(\"jan\", \"feb\", \"mar\", \"apr\", \"may\", \"jun\", \"jul\", \"aug\", \"sep\", \"oct\", \"nov\", \"dec\")\n\nval dfWithMonths = \nmonths\n.zipWithIndex\n.foldLeft(df) {\n   case (tempDf, (month, idx)) => tempDf.withColumn(s\"salary_$month\", col(\"salary\").getItem(idx))\n}","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"39f430f612674268bd4a3","status":404},{"text":"%spark\n\n- create spark session\n\n\nval data = Seq(\nRow(\"james\",\"sales\",Seq(1000,1000,1000,10000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000)),\nRow(\"Michael\",\"sales\",Seq(1400,1400,1400,1400,1400,1900,1900,1900,1900,1900,1900,1900)),\nRow(\"Robert\",\"sales\",Seq(1000,1000,1000,10000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000)),\nRow(\"Saif\",\"Sales\",Seq(1300,1300,1300,1300,1300,1300,1300,1300,1300,1300,1300,1300)),\nRow(\"Maria\",\"Finance\",Seq(1000,1000,1000,10000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000)),\nRow(\"Scott\",\"Finance\",Seq(1000,1000,1000,10000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000)),\nRow(\"Jen\",\"Marketing\",Seq(1000,1000,1000,10000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000)),\nRow(\"Kumar\",\"Marketing\",Seq(1000,1000,1000,10000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000,12000))\n)\n\n\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.types.{StructField,StructType,StringType,ArrayType,DoubleType,IntegerType}\nval schema = StructType(\n  List(\n    StructField(\"employeeName\",StringType,false),\n    StructField(\"department\",StringType,false),\n    StructField(\"salary\", ArrayType(IntegerType),false)\n  )\n)\n\n\nval df = spark.createDataFrame(\n  spark.sparkContext.parallelize(data),\n  schema\n)","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"7e83d6d674bc47dcaf46b","status":404},{"text":"%spark\ndisplay(df1)","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"fab0f538a6664ba5b69c7","status":404},{"text":"%spark\ndisplay(paymentDf)","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"25d59f3e61eb448c8eceb","status":404},{"text":"%spark\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions.{sum}\n\ndf.withColumn(\"sumOfSalary\", expr(\"aggregate(salary, 0D, (acc, x) -> acc + x) as salary_sum\")).show","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"dfc951e7ffe347859309e","status":404},{"text":"%spark\nval x = 10\nval y = true\nval z = if(x == 10) y else x","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"acd48903186648e4b6007","status":404},{"text":"\n1.  list1 = [\"M\", \"na\", \"i\", \"Ke\"]\n    list2 = [\"y\", \"me\", \"s\", \"lly\"]\n\no/p: ['My', 'name', 'is', 'Kelly']\n\n\n2. turn every item of a list into its square, using higer order function\nnumbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]   \n\n  list(map(lambda x: x*x , numbers))\n\n3. list1 = [\"Mike\", \"\", \"Emma\", \"Kelly\", \"\", \"Brad\"]\n\n# remove None from list1 and convert result into list\nres = list(filter(None, list1))\n\n\n4. print history\nsampleDict = {\n    \"class\": {\n        \"student\": {\n            \"name\": \"Mike\",\n            \"marks\": {\n                \"physics\": 70,\n                \"history\": 80\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n5. List Comprehension? Give an Example.\n\nmy_list = [i for i in range(1, 10)]\n\n6. What is a pass in Python?\n\n7. What is the difference between xrange and range functions?\n\n8. What are unit tests in Python? did you used it.\n\n9. exception\n\n   A.  TypeError \n    x = 5\ny = \"hello\"\ntry:\n    z = x + y\nexcept TypeError:\n\n  B. NameError : when variable or funciton not found\n  C. KeyError: This exception is raised when a key is not found in a dictionary.\n  D. ValueError: This exception is raised when a function or method is called with an invalid argument or input, such as trying to convert a string to an integer when the string does not represent a valid integer.\n\n\n      ","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"e588af0fdbde4d149d779","status":404},{"text":"%spark\n","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"792886f8aa46485d95e77","status":404},{"text":"%spark\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions.col\n\ndf1.join(df2,df1.col(\"value1\") === df2.col(\"value2\"),\"left\").show\n\ndf1.join(df2,df1.col(\"value1\") === df2.col(\"value2\"),\"right\").show\n\ndf1.join(df2,df1.col(\"value1\") === df2.col(\"value2\"),\"leftanti\").show\n\ndf1.join(df2,df1.col(\"value1\") === df2.col(\"value2\"),\"leftsemi\").show\n","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"ba1726a3c418426fa360a","status":404},{"text":"%spark\n","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"91b090d5c3ca40279a1fd","status":404},{"text":"%spark\nparsedFile.show","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"d97a6da0934d49dba89cb","status":404},{"text":"%spark\n","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"cb1ce7114e8544ea8297a","status":404},{"text":"### rdd way","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"bf6b61c38ba24a2e81544","status":404},{"text":"%spark\ndbutils.fs.head(\"dbfs:/FileStore/tables/suankiData/raw/interview.txt\")","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"eb0a6434c55c4a9b9e2e1","status":404},{"text":"%spark\nval df1 = Seq(\"A\",\"B\",\"C\",\"C\",\"F\").toDF(\"value1\")\nval df2 = Seq(\"A\",\"A\",\"C\",\"D\",\"E\",\"G\").toDF(\"value2\")\n\n\ndisplay(df2)\n\n","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"ce8dc97ee4404161969bd","status":404},{"text":"%spark\n\n\nval yearWiseDf = df\n.select(col(\"payment_amount\"), year(to_date(col(\"payment_date\"))).alias(\"year\"), lit(null).as(\"store_id\"))\n.groupBy(col(\"year\"),col(\"store_id\")).agg(sum(col(\"payment_amount\")))\n\nval storeWiseDf = df\n.select(col(\"payment_amount\"), lit(null).as(\"year\"),col(\"store_id\"))\n.groupBy(col(\"year\"),col(\"store_id\")).agg(sum(col(\"payment_amount\")))\n\n\nyearWiseDf.show\nstoreWiseDf.show\n\n\ndisplay(yearWiseDf.union(storeWiseDf))\n","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"ba11267db54f4c34b8005","status":404},{"text":"\n1. lazy , var ,val in scala\n\n2. what is auxulary constructor in scala\n\n3. companion object ?\n\nWhat is function composition in Scala?\nfunction currying in Scala ?\n\n4.  Traits and Trait mixin\n\n5. Function literal vs Function vs partial function \n\n6. higher order function\n\nonly square of even numbers\nval l:List[Int] = List(1,2,3,4,5,6)\no/p List(4,16,36)\n\n   -> use higher order funciton to multiply with square\n   -> only even value\n\n7. why case classes are special in scala ? than normal class\n\ncase class Person(name:String)\nclass Human(name:String)\n\nval person = Person(\"Ram\")\nval human = new Human(\"Shyam\")\n\n\n8. what is implicts ?\n\nimplicit def doubleToInt(d: Double) = d.toInt\nval x:Int = 42.0\n\n9. Any, Anyval, null ?\n\n\ncase class Animal(name:String)\n","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"926eec8913f749dc9f222","status":404},{"text":"%spark\nval rdd = \nspark.sparkContext.textFile(\"dbfs:/FileStore/tables/suankiData/raw/interview.txt\")\n\n\n  val parsedFile =rdd\n  .filter(_.trim.nonEmpty)\n  .map { line =>\n    val parts = line.trim.split(\"\\\\s+\")\n    (parts(0), parts(1), parts(2))\n  }.toDF(\"id\", \"type_code\", \"location\")","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"68f2b5ff94904940b1cf5","status":404},{"text":"%spark\n  val parsedFileRdd =rdd\n  .filter(_.trim.nonEmpty)\n  .map { line =>\n    (line.substring(0,4), line.substring(10))\n  }\n\n\nparsedFileRdd.collect\n","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"34df8d5126a441a68a213","status":404},{"text":"%run /my_work/CommonUtils/SetupData","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"be1417c1d7504421b67cb","status":404},{"text":"%spark\nparsedFile\n.groupBy(\"id\").agg(collect_set(col(\"location\")))\n.show(false)","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"350b05c7a0274f07ac213","status":404},{"text":"####SPARK","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"1401ce5de0b24f65891a8","status":404},{"text":"%spark\ndfWithMonths.show","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"22cbfa6538cf402cb4686","status":404},{"text":"%spark\n\n// Sample data\nval data = Seq(\n  Row(\"Alice\", 30, Array(1000.0, 1100.0, 1200.0)),\n  Row(\"Bob\", 28, Array(900.0, 950.0, 980.0))\n)\n\n// Define schema\nval schema = StructType(Seq(\n  StructField(\"name\", StringType, nullable = false),\n  StructField(\"age\", IntegerType, nullable = false),\n  StructField(\"salary\", ArrayType(DoubleType), nullable = false)\n))\n\n// Create DataFrame\nval df = spark.createDataFrame(\n  spark.sparkContext.parallelize(data),\n  schema\n)","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"7f386cedebd849cd81085","status":404},{"text":"\n####PYTHON\n\n","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"493d8bc127a84174afc15","status":404},{"text":"%spark\ndisplay(df)","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"29da90642b4c49aeb9005","status":404},{"text":"%spark\nparsedFileRdd\n.groupByKey()\n.map(x => (x._1,Set(x._2)))\n.collect","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"1cc56728f0074e3bbb9be","status":404},{"text":"%spark\nwrite a Higher order function to calculate only square of even number\n\nval l:List[Int] = List(1,2,3,4,5,6)\n\n//o/p  List( 4,  16,  36)\n","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"b2137d4f3a2c455b91662","status":404},{"text":"%spark\nval paymentDf = spark.sql(\"select * from payment\")","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"85cb0a1193ba4b95a7699","status":404},{"text":"\nspark:\n\n1.  file type ?\nread a csv file from spark ?\n\n2. Explain the execution process of above. \n\n   how many job and stage  would be created\n    val d = spark.read.csv(\"filePath\")\n    d.count()\n\n3. how to handle error records in spark.\n    readMode\n    writeMode\n\n3. lazy evaluation and it's advantage and disadvantage ?\n\n4. what is transformation ?\n  in memory processing vs  \n  Shuffle  durring transformation ?\n\n5. create a sample rdd with 2 partitions.\n\n6. spark.sql.shuffle.partitoins ?\n\n7. what is adaptive query execution ? give example\n   spark.sql.adaptive.enabled?\n\n   heared this ? spark.sql.adaptive.skewedJoin.enabled ,true\n\n    - read run time statistics of data actually no of bytes read and no of partions\n    - tune shuffle partitons based on distinct keys and coalesce the partions, suppose we have only 15 distinct key it would - - coalesce 200 to 15 partions\n    - convert sort merge join to Broadcast join\n    - optimize skew joins by breaking bigger partions into smaller one\n\n8. sort merge join Vs BroadcastHashJoin\n\n9. partition prunning static vs dynamic ? explain\n   -> pushed down filter\n\n9. different type of join\n\ninner, left , right, left semi(all the matched column from left), left anti(only unmatched column)\n\n\nTable A. Table B\t\nA\t  A\nA \tB\nB\t  C\nC\t  D\nC\t  E\n\n\n\n+------+--------+---------------+-----------+-----------+------+------+\n|emp_id|name    |superior_emp_id|year_joined|emp_dept_id|gender|salary|\n+------+--------+---------------+-----------+-----------+------+------+\n|1     |Smith   |-1             |2018       |10         |M     |3000  |\n|2     |Rose    |1              |2010       |20         |M     |4000  |\n|3     |Williams|1              |2010       |10         |M     |1000  |\n|4     |Jones   |2              |2005       |10         |F     |2000  |\n|5     |Brown   |2              |2010       |40         |      |-1    |\n|6     |Brown   |2              |2010       |50         |      |-1    |\n+------+--------+---------------+-----------+-----------+------+------+\n\n+---------+-------+\n|dept_name|dept_id|\n+---------+-------+\n|Finance  |10     |\n|Marketing|20     |\n|Sales    |30     |\n|IT       |40     |\n|IT       |40     |\n+---------+-------+\n\n10. what is sqew join how to handle them\n  \n  aqe ?\n","config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","editorSetting":{"params":{},"forms":{},"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"id":"0adfbc520de7464493548","status":404}],"info":{},"noteForms":{},"noteParams":{},"angularObjects":{}}